    "explanation": "Both sides agree on the physical facts and so do I. The driver's own trace places him 24.01 m from the Tampines MRT Exit D pickup pin, stationary (0.0 km/h on all 34 fixes), from 18:20:00 until he cancelled at 18:25:30 — one continuous in-geofence run of 330 seconds against the 300-second TRANSPORT_HUB minimum. The arrived marker at 18:20:20 is true (he was neither beyond 300 m nor in motion), so POL-NS-05 does not bite and there is no false-arrival event to refer. The SGD 6.00 fee is the greater of the zone-class fee (TRANSPORT_HUB, SGD 6.00) and the vehicle-tier fee (RYDE_PLUS, SGD 6.00) — a tie at SGD 6.00 — so the fare line reconciles and POL-NS-08(d) is not engaged. On that footing POL-NS-01 limbs (a) to (d) are met, and standing alone the charge would hold with SGD 4.80 to the driver under POL-NS-07 (80% of SGD 6.00; the anti-farming check does not trip — 1 no-show termination in 30 days, below 4, and 1/120 = 0.008, below 0.08).\n\nBut POL-NS-01 makes the fee chargeable only if no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, and POL-NS-04 does. All three of its limbs are made out on weight-1.0 artifacts. (a) The chat log shows the rider sending locating messages inside the waiting window at 18:21:00 ('I am at Exit D under the green sign. Where is your car?') and 18:23:25 ('I still cannot see you. Please reply.'). (b) The driver posted no reply within 120 seconds of either and trip_record.in_app_calls is empty — the read receipts show he opened both messages, at 18:21:15 and 18:23:40, and stayed silent until he cancelled. (c) The rider track is present and places her device 41.9 m from the pin on all 16 qualifying fixes, 100% inside the 200 m TRANSPORT_HUB presence radius, well over the majority the limb requires. POL-NS-04 therefore exonerates the rider: the contested SGD 6.00 is refunded in full and no driver compensation is payable. The driver's POL-NS-07 claim for SGD 4.80 is outweighed by exactly this: the condition it depends on — that no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces POL-NS-01 — fails. The driver's own alternative submission, that POL-NS-04 carries the fee to a full refund, is correct.\n\nOn the quality of the evidence: no artifact that carries the refund is impaired under POL-NS-08 — no clock skew (the 18:20:20 arrived event coincides with a fix), no trace gap (34 fixes at a 10 s interval, max_gap_sec 0.0, rider track present), no chat defect (3 messages matching chat_message_count 3, unbroken msg_id sequence), no fare defect. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09106-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 and carries nothing; the rider's claim resting on its absence was already discarded for failing to name its issue code, and nothing here needs an advisory, since no limb of POL-NS-04 turns on one. The rider's mention of prior_no_show_flags is context-only under POL-GEN-01: the claim invokes those lifetime counters only to say they are not substitutes for the citable trailing-window fields, which is correct, so no finding is built on them.\n\nNo escalation applies: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; the admissible artifacts do not contradict one another on arrival, dwell or rider presence; disputes_with_counterparty_90d are 0 for both parties; no_show_disputes_30d is 0; the anti-farming check does not trip; and no deciding fact rests solely on an impaired artifact. No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty."
